From: mdpicoem PicoGUS Integration <martingdavidson@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-04-25
Subject: [PATCH] gus+adlib: optional CSV tap of GUS and OPL3 port I/O

Adds a lightweight, env-gated hook to DOSBox-X's GUS and OPL3/Adlib
read/write paths that logs every port access to a CSV file. Used by
the mdpicoem `picogus_diff_rp2040` harness to drive PicoGUS firmware
inside the RP2040 emulator, and (Phase E) PicoGUS-FM firmware that
also responds to OPL3 port writes.

Activation: set PICOGUS_TAP_FILE=<path> in the environment before
launching DOSBox-X. If unset, no tap; both code paths are unchanged
at runtime. A single trace captures both buses, time-sorted by ns.

Format (one event per line, matching HLD Stage 3):

    # picogus-tap v1
    ns,port,value,kind
    0,0x243,0x00,write8
    1234567,0x388,0x20,write8
    1234890,0x389,0x01,write8

`ns` is derived from PIC_FullIndex() (milliseconds * 1e6), `port` is
the full 12-bit decoded ISA port, `value` is 0x%02x for width-1 or
0x%04x for width-2, `kind` is write8|write16|read8|read16.

Files touched:
  - src/hardware/gus.cpp  : tap helpers (file-scope state) + GUS hooks.
                            picogus_tap_log() is non-static so adlib.cpp
                            can call it; other helpers stay file-local.
  - src/hardware/adlib.cpp: extern decl of picogus_tap_log + log calls
                            in OPL_Read (post-PortRead) and OPL_Write
                            (post-PC98 port-shift). Adlib registers with
                            IO_MB only, so iolen is 1 in practice; the
                            ternary mirrors the GUS hook's wider invariant.
                            No reentrancy guard needed -- Module::PortRead
                            does not decompose 16-bit reads.

The file is fopen'd once lazily on the first access (from either bus),
fflushed per line, and closed at process exit (via static lifetime).

Apply with `git apply third_party/dosbox-x-picogus-tap.patch` or
`patch -p1 -F5 --no-backup-if-mismatch`.

---
 src/hardware/adlib.cpp |  26 ++++++++-
 src/hardware/gus.cpp   | 147 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 162 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

